@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# Cluster source audit and correctness checkpoint
+
+Date: 2026-10-12 (Asia/Seoul). Baseline commit: `a998077419fd59d91141ce2b9b1fe48ae0d2d7aa`. The working tree was clean before the audit. This checkpoint contains fixes and regressions, not a production certification. No dependencies were added.
+
+## Reproducible verification
+
+Baseline commands all succeeded: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (262 library tests), `cargo build --release`. Their unedited output is in [baseline-fmt.log](baseline-fmt.log), [baseline-clippy.log](baseline-clippy.log), [baseline-test.log](baseline-test.log), and [baseline-release.log](baseline-release.log). Passing existing tests did not establish the invariants below.
+
+Final commands, exit codes, elapsed time and log paths are recorded in [verification.json](verification.json). Final `cargo test --all-targets` reports **295 passed; 0 failed** in the library, plus successful binary, example and Criterion target executions. The 33 new `audit_` tests include numerical, data, hardware and PCB cases. Existing PCB connectivity fixtures that used unknown footprints/body origins were updated to known resistor footprints and their real pad positions; their former origin-fallback expectation was itself the defective behavior. The full output is [final-test.log](final-test.log). `cargo check`, formatting, all-target/all-feature Clippy and release also succeeded. No desktop GUI, firmware compiler, physical hardware, external Gerber viewer or fabrication service was exercised.
+
+## Invariant coverage
+
+| Invariant | Actual source examined and evidence | Result / boundary |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1. Schematic endpoint identity | `engine/netlist.rs` canonical pipeline; `model/project.rs` attachment index; `commands/component.rs::Paste` | Paste now remaps typed pin identities instead of discarding them. Existing component-move/delete tests exercise attachment preservation. |
+| 2. Intersections / deterministic nets | `engine/netlist.rs` normalization, endpoint resolution, union/find, label projection | Existing exact-map tests cover crossings without dots, explicit dots, T branches, overlap, shared junctions and input-order independence. These working modules were preserved. This is bounded regression evidence, not a proof over all geometry. |
+| 3. ERC assumptions | `engine/erc/rules/beginner.rs::pin_is_5v_source`, `check_esp_gpio_overvoltage` | A negative source terminal no longer counts as a 5V driver. STM32 conditional/unknown tolerance produces uncertainty rather than an unjustified definitive error. |
+| 4. MNA | `engine/mna/{matrix,dc,ac}.rs` | Fixed reference-node selection, zero/near-zero stamping, numerical scaling/nonfinite handling, source cycles and AC source constraints. See electrical report. |
+| 5. Nonlinear approximations | `engine/mna/dc.rs` state iteration (24 iterations), diode/MOS piecewise models; `engine/transient.rs` analytic RC | RC now requires a real charging loop and rejects extra storage. Diode/MOS/AC model accuracy remains educational. |
+| 6. Simulation caches | `app/actions.rs::current_netlist`, `current_simulation`, `poll_analysis_worker`; `engine/worker.rs::execute` | Property projection is refreshed separately from canonical topology. ERC cache includes electrical revision because several nominally structural rules read values. |
+| 7. MCU metadata | `model/device.rs::board_profile`, `pin_capability`; inspector in `ui/app/mod.rs` | Partial source-backed profiles distinguish GPIO/header/package/ratings. Unknown facts stay unknown. See coverage matrix in electrical report. |
+| 8. PCB pad mapping | `pcb/copper.rs::resolve_pads` | Per-instance mapping replaces footprint-origin terminals and library-level net assignment. Every schematic pin must map; unknown pins block export. |
+| 9. Copper islands | `pcb/copper.rs::pad_islands`, `pcb/board.rs::ratsnest_edges` | Actual copper overlap and layers govern connectivity; same-footprint pads do not automatically connect. Four tests also failed against the original baseline source. |
+| 10. DRC geometry | `pcb/geometry.rs`; `pcb/drc.rs::{run_drc,run_drc_with_nets}`; `pcb/board.rs::valid_polygon` | Concave outlines and copper extents are checked; pad/copper pairs use shared shape distances. Local interactive checks remain a subset; export runs fresh full checks. |
+| 11. Manufacturing | `export/gerber.rs`; `app/actions.rs::export_pcb_fabrication_files` | Apertures, pad shapes, via copper, units and mirrored/rotated drills corrected and golden-tested. Output explicitly experimental. |
+| 12. ECO | `pcb/board.rs::{eco_report,apply_eco_patch,remap_copper_nets}` | Copper is remapped by old pin identities. Splits/unknowns become unverified orphans. Footprint placement stays in place; replacing a package still requires user review. |
+| 13. Undo/redo | `editor/delta.rs::BoardMetadata`; `commands/pcb.rs` ECO capture; paste transaction | ECO copper net changes and bindings enter reversible deltas. Paste is a single undoable operation. Memory estimates include new bindings but are still approximate. |
+| 14. Persistence | `app/actions.rs` project-folder save/load and SavedCircuit conversion; `storage/save.rs` atomic writer | One authoritative project snapshot prevents torn schematic/board mirror loads. Autosave now includes PCB. Future schema/exhausted IDs reject before replacement; allocator round trips remain stable. |
+| 15. UI mutations | `app/command_dispatch.rs`, `commands/properties.rs`, `ui/pcb_workspace.rs`, revision-tagged worker | Manual routing starts at the clicked pad/net/layer. Local DRC schedules full validation. Worker results are gated by revisions. No exhaustive audit of every possible UI event interleaving. |
+| 16. Hot paths | `performance.rs`, `examples/performance_probe.rs`; cached PCB ratsnest | Ratsnest connectivity is cached for painting. Correctness increases full-DRC cost substantially; measured results and remaining quadratic paths are in the performance report. |
+
+Source paths in this table are relative to [src](../../src). Relevant implementations and their regression tests are specified in the companion reports.
+
+## Confirmed data/editor defects corrected
+
+All entries describe pre-correction behavior. New guard defects discovered while implementing this audit are identified separately.
+
+| Severity | Exact file / function | Root cause and reproduction | Correction / regression |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P0 | `app/actions.rs::save_project_folder_to`, `load_project_folder_from` | Independent schematic and board writes could be loaded from different generations. Save then corrupt/change mirror files. | `project.json` contains the complete authoritative commit and is written last; legacy mirrors remain loadable. `audit_project_commit_survives_torn_mirror_files`; [failing-persistence.log](failing-persistence.log). |
+| P0 | `app/actions.rs::SavedCircuit::from_app`, `into_snapshot` | Recovery serialized schematic only; PCB edits disappeared. Save recovery snapshot with a track. | Backward-compatible optional board snapshot and rebuilt lookup indices. `audit_autorecovery_preserves_pcb_edits`; [failing-autorecovery.log](failing-autorecovery.log). |
+| P0 | `app/actions.rs::poll_analysis_worker` | Failed autosave left revision marked submitted, suppressing retry until another edit. Use a regular file as the intended parent directory. | Reset submission watermark after error and keep visible failure status. `audit_autosave_failure_allows_retry_of_same_revision`; [failing-autosave-retry.log](failing-autosave-retry.log). |
+| P0 | `app/actions.rs::repair_saved_page`, `SavedCircuit::into_snapshot` | Maximum IDs overflowed subsequent allocation; normal loads also incremented `next_id` unnecessarily. Load exhausted ID / save-load-save repeatedly. | Headroom check rejects exhausted identities; repair takes max of saved and existing+1. `audit_exhausted_saved_identity_is_rejected_before_mutation`, `audit_save_load_save_preserves_allocator_state`; [failing-persistence.log](failing-persistence.log), [failing-eco-determinism.log](failing-eco-determinism.log). |
+| P1 | `commands/component.rs::ComponentCommand::Paste` | Constructing new wires discarded explicit PinRef endpoints; stale geometric endpoints then disconnected copied subcircuits. | Remap copied PinRefs; detach external references safely to translated points. `audit_paste_remaps_explicit_pin_identity_and_is_atomic`; [failing-paste.log](failing-paste.log). |
+| P0 | `app/actions.rs::current_netlist`, `engine/worker.rs::execute` | Cached topology carried old value/label metadata; ERC structural cache ignored parameter edits. Change source 3.3V to 5V without rewiring. | Overlay fresh component properties and cache them by connectivity/electrical revisions; conservatively refresh structural ERC on electrical edits. `audit_property_changes_refresh_netlist_without_rebuilding_connectivity`, `audit_value_edit_updates_worker_overvoltage_erc`; [failing-property-cache.log](failing-property-cache.log). |
+| P0 | `pcb/board.rs::apply_eco_patch`, `remap_copper_nets` | Numeric net renumbering could attach manual copper to an unrelated net; undo did not retain changed assignment identity. | Persist old pin sets, remap unique surviving/merged nets, orphan ambiguous splits, capture before/after copper. `audit_eco_net_renumbering_preserves_copper_identity_and_undo`; [failing-eco-determinism.log](failing-eco-determinism.log). |
+| P0 | `pcb/board.rs::eco_report` | Removal policy still compared numeric IDs after identity-remapping was introduced; renumbering deleted preserved tracks under explicit removal policy. | Determine removed nets by pin identity when available. `audit_eco_explicit_removal_policy_preserves_renumbered_net`; [failing-eco-removal-policy.log](failing-eco-removal-policy.log). Discovered during this audit implementation. |
+
+A final extension of the ECO test adds a zone to the renumbered net. It reproduced a zone assignment remaining changed after `EcoPatch::rollback`; [failing-eco-zone-undo.log](failing-eco-zone-undo.log) records the failure. `EcoPatch::{rollback,reapply}` now captures/restores zone metadata alongside tracks, vias and bindings. This P0 undo defect was introduced by the new remapping path and corrected before the checkpoint.
+
+The single-file commit improves process-level consistency, but does not establish power-loss durability of directory rename on every filesystem. Corrupt legacy multi-file saves cannot be reconstructed automatically. The remaining-risks report distinguishes these risks from reproduced bugs.
+
+## Reviewable checkpoint
+
+Changes remain in the working tree on the baseline commit. `checkpoint.patch` includes source, reports, fixtures and selected evidence logs and is checked with `git apply --check` against a fresh baseline archive. [checkpoint.json](checkpoint.json) records SHA-256 hashes of changed source/report/fixture files. It is a content checkpoint, not a Git commit. Logs retain the failing reproductions and successful final validation; no claim is made that every suggested adversarial example received a new test.
